<title>UK: BBA buys Trinity Aerospace for 3.7 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BBA buys Trinity Aerospace for 3.7 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engineering group BBA Plc said on Friday it had bought landing gear maintenance company Trinity Aerospace for 3.35 million stg in cash plus the refinancing of 0.31 million in debt.</p>
<p>BBA said in a statement that the company being bought, which had sales in the six months to September 30 of 1.7 million stg, was a complementary fit with its existing APPH Aviation Services business.</p>
<p>&quot;In addition, Trinity adds an enhanced range of metal finishing facilities to the existing BBA business which are not presently available within AAPH,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
